cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use causalkit in research, please cite the software and the exact version used."
type: software
title: "causalkit: Identification-aware causal inference and instrumental variables for Python"
abstract: >-
  An identification-aware Python toolkit for causal inference. Version 0.1.0a1
  provides linear two-stage least squares with an excluded-instrument API,
  homoskedastic, HC1, and one-way cluster-robust covariance, strict data
  contracts, and first-stage and overidentification diagnostics.
authors:
  - family-names: Akanbi
    given-names: "Oluwajuwon Mayomi"
version: 0.1.0a1
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akanom/causalkit"
url: "https://github.com/Akanom/causalkit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - econometrics
  - instrumental variables
  - two-stage least squares
  - 2SLS
  - identification
